WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:11.160
[PIRATE A]
Too bad.

3
00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:13.370
Looks like I win again.

4
00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:16.500
[PERONA]
Hard at work, I see.

5
00:00:16.870 --> 00:00:18.870
Hand over the keys to the cells.

6
00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:20.040
Huh?

7
00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:23.380
Who the hell are you?

8
00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:28.720
Really?

9
00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:43.020
Seems your manners are as foul
as your body odor.

10
00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:45.070
<b>"Ghost Princess" Perona
Hollow-Hollow Fruit</b>

11
00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:47.030
[PIRATE B]
What did you say?

12
00:00:47.030 --> 00:00:49.900
[PIRATE A]
You've got
a lot of nerves, little lady.

13
00:00:51.410 --> 00:00:55.080
[PERONA]
I could say the same about you.
Let's fix that, shall we?

14
00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:02.920
Now kneel before me!

15
00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:05.090
Negative.

16
00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:24.980
[PIRATE B]
I'm not even fit
to be a worm on a fishing hook.

17
00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:29.470
[PIRATE A]
I'm gonna crawl into one
of these prison cells just to hide my shame.

18
00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:38.120
Thank you, boys.

19
00:01:38.120 --> 00:01:40.000
Alright!

20
00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:03.190
Not very lively in here, is it? Huh?

21
00:02:06.020 --> 00:02:07.400
Hey, stop that.

22
00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:10.010
[COBY]
Huh?

23
00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:23.500
Good. Get up.

24
00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:31.340
I know you.

25
00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:37.300
Wait a second. You're Koby the hero.

26
00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:39.260
<b>Captain Koby
Marine Headquarters
(SWORD)</b>

27
00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:45.560
you'll free Master Moria
from his cell, deeper inside.

28
00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:47.520
Moria?

29
00:02:49.640 --> 00:02:51.950
Gecko Moria is being held here?

30
00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:55.450
Wait, are you telling me you want
me to help a notorious criminal escape?

31
00:02:55.820 --> 00:02:57.200
I am, yes.

32
00:02:57.200 --> 00:02:59.660
Because if you don't,
then he'll surely be killed.

33
00:03:04.830 --> 00:03:07.060
How can I set him free?

34
00:04:37.050 --> 00:04:41.430
<b>The Legendary Hero</b>

35
00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:43.220
We got some big

36
00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:47.100
<b>Beehive, the Pirate Island
New World</b>

37
00:04:43.550 --> 00:04:45.890
news! Captain Koby has escaped!

38
00:04:45.890 --> 00:04:47.100
[PIRATE D]
Are you serious?!

39
00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:52.940
the Commodore can't stop us
from goin' after him.

40
00:04:52.940 --> 00:04:55.530
We'll be set for life
if we can catch him ourselves!

41
00:04:55.530 --> 00:05:00.990
[PIRATE F]
Then what the hell are we waitin' for? Alright!
He's already got a bounty, so we'll be good to go!

42
00:05:00.990 --> 00:05:03.490
All we gotta do is take
his head to Cross Guild!

43
00:05:03.490 --> 00:05:06.370
Hell yeah. I bought odds
on him with a Win ticket

44
00:05:06.370 --> 00:05:08.330
and the payout's gonna be huge!

45
00:05:08.330 --> 00:05:10.330
[PIRATE J]
How much
will we get if we kill him?

46
00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:12.630
Heh. You might wanna sit down for this one.

47
00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:16.750
His bounty is five stars!
That means he's worth

48
00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:20.420
five treasure chests... 500 million berries!

49
00:05:20.420 --> 00:05:23.050
Captains are usually only worth one star!

50
00:05:23.050 --> 00:05:25.950
They must really want this guy dead, huh?

51
00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:31.100
[PIRATE L]
Alright, men! The hunt is on!

52
00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:33.980
We're about to hit the jackpot!

53
00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:39.320
[PIZARRO]
I've got an itch
on the left side of my chest.

54
00:05:39.650 --> 00:05:42.950
That's where the slaves are held
before the sale. Huh?

55
00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:51.250
[PIZARRO]
Are you kitten me?
They're escaping!

56
00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:53.750
The slaves are runnin' for it?

57
00:05:53.940 --> 00:05:56.960
Yeah! That means
we can hunt 'em down! Oh, boy!

58
00:05:56.960 --> 00:05:58.590
[PIZARRO]
Don't even think ameowt it!

59
00:05:58.590 --> 00:06:00.420
Keep your claws in check!

60
00:06:00.970 --> 00:06:02.680
Bring 'em back! Now! And you

61
00:06:02.680 --> 00:06:04.140
better not kill Koby!

62
00:06:04.590 --> 00:06:06.220
Or I'll make sure you answer to Teach!

63
00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:11.020
Uh. Wait, did that rock just talk?

64
00:06:11.390 --> 00:06:13.520
[COBY]
No. Pizarro knows that we're here!

65
00:06:13.520 --> 00:06:14.730
We need to run!

66
00:06:19.820 --> 00:06:21.650
[PRISONER C]
We're not gonna make it.

67
00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:26.660
Please, Koby, you need to get out of here
while you still can. Don't let us slow you down.

68
00:06:26.660 --> 00:06:28.870
I promised that I'd help you escape,

69
00:06:28.870 --> 00:06:31.250
and you will, by using me as bait!

70
00:06:31.750 --> 00:06:35.880
Run as fast as you can! And no matter what,
don't let the pirates catch you!

71
00:06:35.880 --> 00:06:36.630
Go!

72
00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:39.900
I'll see you all again soon!

73
00:06:45.010 --> 00:06:47.220
Thank you, Captain Koby.

74
00:06:50.260 --> 00:06:52.600
[PRISONER D]
You're a living saint!

75
00:06:57.560 --> 00:07:00.480
<b>Shiryu of the Rain
Clear-Clear Fruit
Invisible Man</b>

76
00:07:00.480 --> 00:07:05.880
[SHIRYU]
Why don't you capture
the damned slaves yourself, Pizarro?

77
00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:12.410
'Cause I don't want Teach
to come back and chew meowt.

78
00:07:11.870 --> 00:07:15.410
<b>"Corrupt King" Avalo Pizarro
Isle-Isle Fruit
Island Man</b>

79
00:07:15.410 --> 00:07:19.040
[PIZARRO]
Whenever I move too much,
I end up breaking things and it's a huge mess. Hm?

80
00:07:23.260 --> 00:07:25.800
Why don't I stop 'em, huh?

81
00:07:25.800 --> 00:07:29.010
Furget it, Vasco. What are you gonna do?

82
00:07:35.230 --> 00:07:38.980
If I set the town on fire,
they'll have nowhere to run, right?

83
00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:42.070
<b>"Heavy Drinker" Vasco Shot
Glug-Glug Fruit
Booze Man</b>

84
00:07:49.660 --> 00:07:52.990
[PIZARRO]
That would be a complete
cat-tastrophe! Don't you dare!

85
00:07:53.330 --> 00:07:55.450
Teach is gonna be furry-ous!

86
00:07:55.450 --> 00:07:58.210
[VASCO]
Eh, what's that? Burn 'em, you said?

87
00:07:58.710 --> 00:08:03.300
[PIZARRO]
Absolutely no burning anyone, you hear me?
We just finished repairing Rocky Port!

88
00:08:03.800 --> 00:08:07.170
Alright, have it your way.
We'll let Wolf handle it.

89
00:08:10.070 --> 00:08:12.760
[PIZARRO]
Wait, Wolf?

90
00:08:12.760 --> 00:08:16.980
<b>"Colossal Battleship" Sanjuan Wolf
Huge-Huge Fruit
Gigantification Man</b>

91
00:08:14.640 --> 00:08:16.980
[PIZARRO]
That's
the worst idea I've ever heard!

92
00:08:16.980 --> 00:08:19.980
He'll crush the whole town into kitty litter!

93
00:08:24.610 --> 00:08:25.690
Over here!

94
00:08:29.840 --> 00:08:33.700
Damn it, what am I supposed to do now?
I can't keep running away forever!

95
00:08:36.200 --> 00:08:37.160
I'll be okay.

96
00:08:38.210 --> 00:08:43.500
I just have to hold out until the others can get out of here.
I'll figure out the rest after that!

97
00:08:45.880 --> 00:08:47.880
Well, well. Koby the Hero!

98
00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:57.330
I'm so glad you're here, Koby.
'Cause I've got big plans.

99
00:08:58.100 --> 00:09:00.940
I'm gonna turn Pirate Island...

100
00:09:01.310 --> 00:09:05.150
...into a full-fledged country!

101
00:09:05.150 --> 00:09:09.360
One that flies the flag
of the World Government!

102
00:09:10.610 --> 00:09:12.320
And that'll make me a king

103
00:09:12.660 --> 00:09:14.700
of the Blackbeard Kingdom!

104
00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:20.120
So what d'you think?

105
00:09:20.120 --> 00:09:22.210
I think your plan's as ridiculous as you are.

106
00:09:22.580 --> 00:09:24.710
You really think the Government
would agree to that?

107
00:09:25.130 --> 00:09:27.170
To a country made up of criminals?

108
00:09:27.550 --> 00:09:31.550
Hey! Don't you know it's rude
to stomp on someone's dream?

109
00:09:31.550 --> 00:09:35.550
They might see it my way,
now I've got you as a bargaining chip.

110
00:09:36.850 --> 00:09:40.600
The day the Navy negotiates
with terrorists will be the day justice dies!

111
00:09:41.440 --> 00:09:43.940
And I won't be your bargaining chip.

112
00:09:44.810 --> 00:09:45.860
I can't be.

113
00:09:46.570 --> 00:09:48.530
I'm a member of SWORD!

114
00:09:49.780 --> 00:09:51.610
Huh? The hell is SWORD?

115
00:09:51.610 --> 00:09:53.320
Never heard of it.

116
00:09:53.320 --> 00:09:54.870
[AOKIJI]
So that's how it is.

117
00:09:54.870 --> 00:09:55.570
Huh?

118
00:09:55.570 --> 00:09:57.580
This will not end well.

119
00:09:57.580 --> 00:09:59.910
Call off the trade, Teach. It won't work.

120
00:10:00.340 --> 00:10:02.320
Huh?

121
00:10:07.590 --> 00:10:09.130
Since this kid's from SWORD,

122
00:10:09.130 --> 00:10:12.170
that means he's a Marine, but not officially.

123
00:10:13.470 --> 00:10:15.930
SWORD members surrender their Navy Code.

124
00:10:18.140 --> 00:10:23.100
They aren't like their comrades.
They're Marines who have submitted their resignations.

125
00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:27.270
They can pick fights with the Four Emperors
without permission from above.

126
00:10:27.270 --> 00:10:31.610
They can also disregard orders
at their discretion and move as they like.

127
00:10:33.320 --> 00:10:34.820
And that's the issue.

128
00:10:36.030 --> 00:10:39.870
The Navy is absolved
of all responsibility for their actions.

129
00:10:40.490 --> 00:10:43.390
They can cut them loose as they see fit.

130
00:10:45.210 --> 00:10:46.580
[TEACH]
Ain't that cute!

131
00:10:47.080 --> 00:10:50.840
Most Marines just sit on their asses,
waiting for daddy's permission to fight us.

132
00:10:51.260 --> 00:10:54.680
But you do what you like,
consequences be damned!

133
00:10:56.330 --> 00:10:59.810
I get it now! I like your style!

134
00:11:01.100 --> 00:11:02.140
That said,

135
00:11:02.140 --> 00:11:04.770
I'm not gonna change my plan!

136
00:11:05.350 --> 00:11:07.890
'Cause you're a special case!

137
00:11:08.360 --> 00:11:10.570
Doesn't matter if you're with SWORD or not.

138
00:11:11.280 --> 00:11:14.820
The public won't like it
if the Navy abandons you.

139
00:11:14.820 --> 00:11:18.240
It's bad press to turn your back on a hero, right?

140
00:11:19.030 --> 00:11:21.490
Your life's in the people's hands.

141
00:11:22.620 --> 00:11:25.660
Looks like the World Government
will lose credibility either way!

142
00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:32.570
I think he gets the message. We're done here.

143
00:11:33.170 --> 00:11:35.010
Lock him up

144
00:11:35.010 --> 00:11:37.720
and don't let him escape!

145
00:11:39.470 --> 00:11:42.310
[PIRATE R]
Get back here, Koby!

146
00:11:47.920 --> 00:11:49.360
[PERONA]
Here's the deal.

147
00:11:49.360 --> 00:11:55.650
I'll unlock this door for you, and in return,

148
00:11:55.650 --> 00:11:58.450
[COBY]
Guess this is what
I deserve for helping a pirate!

149
00:11:58.950 --> 00:12:01.330
But necessity knows no law!

150
00:12:06.430 --> 00:12:07.480
Huh?

151
00:12:08.870 --> 00:12:09.790
[PIRATE S]
The hell's that?

152
00:12:19.470 --> 00:12:22.180
[PIRATE T]
Three Marines
just showed up at the port!

153
00:12:22.680 --> 00:12:25.220
Huh? Marines? That can't be!

154
00:12:25.850 --> 00:12:27.180
[PIRATE U]
Hurry up!

155
00:12:28.230 --> 00:12:30.810
[PIRATE V]
They're strong! Be careful!

156
00:12:32.610 --> 00:12:34.730
[COBY]
Did someone come to rescue me?

157
00:12:34.730 --> 00:12:36.070
No, stop it, Koby, this

158
00:12:36.070 --> 00:12:37.740
is not the time for your selfishness!

159
00:12:37.740 --> 00:12:38.950
What is wrong with me?

160
00:12:58.630 --> 00:12:59.760
[PIRATE AB]
Who are they?

161
00:12:59.760 --> 00:13:01.260
They're monsters!

162
00:13:01.260 --> 00:13:03.760
[PIRATE AC]
Looks like they're headed
straight to the center of town!

163
00:13:03.760 --> 00:13:04.720
What do they want from us?

164
00:13:04.720 --> 00:13:07.140
I don't know! Just shoot!

165
00:13:14.730 --> 00:13:15.730
What?

166
00:13:15.730 --> 00:13:17.190
They didn't even flinch!

167
00:13:18.650 --> 00:13:20.990
[PIRATE AD]
End of the line, monster!

168
00:13:23.570 --> 00:13:25.990
[PIRATE AE]
Whoa! His head came off!

169
00:13:28.520 --> 00:13:32.210
[PIRATE AD]
Woohoo!
Y'see that? That's how it's done!

170
00:13:32.540 --> 00:13:33.920
They're not so tough now!

171
00:13:40.510 --> 00:13:41.800
[MARINE GOLEM A]
That hurt.

172
00:13:42.800 --> 00:13:43.930
Huh? He's a logia-type!

173
00:13:44.260 --> 00:13:45.800
[PIRATE AD]
What the hell is wrong with him?

174
00:13:45.800 --> 00:13:48.100
His body's like clay!

175
00:13:49.640 --> 00:13:52.020
[PIRATE F]
Where are you, Koby?!

176
00:13:54.230 --> 00:13:55.980
Hey, look over there!

177
00:13:56.360 --> 00:13:58.730
I swear I just saw
those buildings move on their own!

178
00:13:58.730 --> 00:14:00.490
Yeah, sure they did, pal!

179
00:14:00.490 --> 00:14:02.450
How's quitting drinking going for ya?

180
00:14:09.790 --> 00:14:12.960
[KUJAKU]
Be good and do as I say!

181
00:14:15.380 --> 00:14:17.130
Now march forward!

182
00:14:17.130 --> 00:14:20.090
Is she whipping that building? That's weird.

183
00:14:20.090 --> 00:14:22.880
Come on. Where's your stamina?

184
00:14:25.180 --> 00:14:27.510
[KUJAKU]
Is that really the best you can do?

185
00:14:27.510 --> 00:14:29.640
You are so pathetic!

186
00:14:29.640 --> 00:14:32.140
[PIRATE AJ]
I kinda feel
like we shouldn't be watching this.

187
00:14:33.350 --> 00:14:35.560
Hi, boys. Finished staring?

188
00:14:35.560 --> 00:14:37.270
Uh! We, uh...

189
00:14:37.820 --> 00:14:39.980
Wait, that mark!

190
00:14:46.740 --> 00:14:50.410
You pirates act like
you've never seen a Marine before.

191
00:14:49.950 --> 00:14:53.410
<b>Rear Admiral Kujaku
Marine Headquarters (SWORD)
Granddaughter of "Master Tactician" Tsuru
Whip-Whip Fruit
Discipline Woman</b>

192
00:14:53.410 --> 00:14:55.670
[KUJAKU]
How adorable.

193
00:14:55.670 --> 00:14:57.170
Come here.

194
00:15:04.760 --> 00:15:06.640
Let me teach you a lesson.

195
00:15:16.480 --> 00:15:18.610
[COBY]
What now? I'm done for!

196
00:15:23.250 --> 00:15:25.280
[PIRATE AL]
Eyes on the target, boys!

197
00:15:28.990 --> 00:15:30.700
Ready. Aim.

198
00:15:30.700 --> 00:15:33.290
Fire!

199
00:15:45.010 --> 00:15:45.590
Huh?

200
00:15:53.350 --> 00:15:56.440
[PIRATE C]
What? What?

201
00:15:56.440 --> 00:15:57.810
What?

202
00:16:00.170 --> 00:16:02.980
Oh, my! How lovely!

203
00:16:02.980 --> 00:16:04.070
Wait, no!

204
00:16:04.070 --> 00:16:05.440
What is this?

205
00:16:05.860 --> 00:16:08.200
Where are these goddamn flowers coming from?

206
00:16:09.450 --> 00:16:11.700
Wait, I've seen this.

207
00:16:11.700 --> 00:16:12.870
Of course!

208
00:16:15.530 --> 00:16:18.170
[PIRATE D]
Dr. Vegapunk invented this!

209
00:16:22.590 --> 00:16:25.710
[PIRATE D]
In fact,
it earned him the Mobel Peace Prize!

210
00:16:26.760 --> 00:16:28.840
Nobody cares about that, okay?!

211
00:16:29.470 --> 00:16:31.800
Who the hell did this to our guns?

212
00:16:31.800 --> 00:16:33.010
Hey, Koby!

213
00:16:36.430 --> 00:16:38.440
[HIBARI]
Come here and stay close to me!

214
00:16:39.770 --> 00:16:41.360
Uh. Uh. But not in a weird way!

215
00:16:41.520 --> 00:16:45.320
<b>Commander Hibari
Marine Headquarters
(SWORD)</b>

216
00:16:45.320 --> 00:16:48.110
Wait, Hibari? What are you doing here?

217
00:16:48.650 --> 00:16:49.740
Are those...?

218
00:16:49.740 --> 00:16:50.860
That's right.

219
00:16:50.860 --> 00:16:54.450
They're Flower Rounds.
But they won't last; we have to hurry!

220
00:16:54.790 --> 00:16:56.950
We need to go before the enemy's gunpowder

221
00:16:56.950 --> 00:16:58.910
stops turning into flowers!

222
00:16:59.370 --> 00:17:01.790
Also... I, uh...

223
00:17:01.790 --> 00:17:03.630
I don't want your food to get cold!

224
00:17:04.000 --> 00:17:05.250
Because I... I...

225
00:17:06.630 --> 00:17:08.010
I packed you a lunch!

226
00:17:08.010 --> 00:17:09.090
[COBY]
Huh?

227
00:17:09.090 --> 00:17:12.360
[HIBARI]
Ah! No, I misspoke!
I mean, you misheard me!

228
00:17:18.620 --> 00:17:20.560
[TASHIGI]
Prince! What's the status?

229
00:17:21.210 --> 00:17:24.770
[GRUS]
We're in the clear.
Everything went off without a hitch.

230
00:17:28.440 --> 00:17:32.200
<b>Rear Admiral Prince Grus</b>
<b>Marine Headquarters</b>

231
00:17:32.200 --> 00:17:34.660
<b>Glorp-Glorp Fruit</b>
<b>Clay Man</b>

232
00:17:32.200 --> 00:17:34.070
Koby's doing fine!

233
00:17:34.660 --> 00:17:37.120
<b>Mud Puppet (Golem)</b>

234
00:17:37.490 --> 00:17:40.960
Wait a sec. This place
doesn't look right. Where are we?

235
00:17:40.960 --> 00:17:41.580
Huh?

236
00:17:43.150 --> 00:17:47.300
Hey! Everyone, look!
That building just moved!

237
00:17:47.300 --> 00:17:48.760
[PIRATE G]
No! Wait!

238
00:17:52.090 --> 00:17:53.800
It's too late.

239
00:17:53.800 --> 00:17:55.890
They moved the buildings
and trapped us here!

240
00:17:55.890 --> 00:17:57.890
Whenever you're ready!

241
00:17:58.270 --> 00:17:59.850
Aim for the dead center!

242
00:18:00.230 --> 00:18:02.190
I just got confirmation from Prince!

243
00:18:02.520 --> 00:18:03.940
Everyone is in position!

244
00:18:03.940 --> 00:18:06.120
We're ready, Vice Admiral!

245
00:18:06.900 --> 00:18:09.440
Everyone! Hang on tight!

246
00:18:12.030 --> 00:18:14.320
To hell we go!

247
00:18:22.620 --> 00:18:23.960
Okay, hurry.

248
00:18:24.370 --> 00:18:26.210
Alright! If you're ready, I am, too!

249
00:18:27.990 --> 00:18:29.960
Whoa, what the hell is that?

250
00:18:29.960 --> 00:18:33.470
I'm not stickin' around to find out!

251
00:18:47.440 --> 00:18:51.320
[PIRATE K]
There's an alien ship in the sky!
It's flying straight for us!

252
00:18:51.320 --> 00:18:53.990
[PIRATE L]
But why? And how?

253
00:18:53.990 --> 00:18:55.320
[PIRATE M]
Whose ship is that?

254
00:18:56.780 --> 00:18:59.700
Huh... Looks like it's falling.

255
00:18:59.700 --> 00:19:02.250
[PIRATE O]
We gotta go! Run away!

256
00:19:05.960 --> 00:19:07.080
[PIRATE P]
No way!

257
00:19:07.080 --> 00:19:08.590
I know that ship!

258
00:19:11.380 --> 00:19:14.840
[PIRATE Q]
No. That can't be right!
I thought he retired!

259
00:19:15.340 --> 00:19:16.800
[PIRATE R]
The legendary hero!

260
00:19:16.800 --> 00:19:18.390
He's coming!

261
00:19:22.900 --> 00:19:26.480
It's Vice Admiral Garp!

262
00:19:26.980 --> 00:19:28.480
Koby!

263
00:19:28.480 --> 00:19:30.480
Koby! I came to get ya, boy!

264
00:19:32.230 --> 00:19:34.990
Come on! We have to take cover!

265
00:19:34.990 --> 00:19:35.950
We're trapped!

266
00:19:35.950 --> 00:19:37.910
There's no way outta here!

267
00:19:41.490 --> 00:19:45.040
What?! You wanna piece of me?!

268
00:19:45.870 --> 00:19:48.000
Uh! Oh, shit! – He's coming for us!

269
00:20:06.890 --> 00:20:08.770
I'm not worth any of this!

270
00:20:09.810 --> 00:20:12.900
You would risk starting a war
just to protect me?

271
00:20:13.320 --> 00:20:14.900
Hey, morons!

272
00:20:15.610 --> 00:20:20.870
Who do you think you kidnapped?
Do you know who that kid is?

273
00:20:28.960 --> 00:20:32.170
[GARP]
Koby's not
just the future of the Navy!

274
00:20:33.340 --> 00:20:35.960
That boy

275
00:20:36.420 --> 00:20:40.550
is my favorite student!

276
00:20:41.930 --> 00:20:45.220
Galaxy...

277
00:20:56.400 --> 00:21:00.280
Impact!

278
00:22:14.600 --> 00:22:16.610
My back! Damn Garp!

279
00:22:16.610 --> 00:22:18.190
He's insane!

280
00:22:18.190 --> 00:22:20.440
Where'd ya go? You're dead!

281
00:22:20.440 --> 00:22:22.800
Hey, pirates! Not so fast!

282
00:22:23.110 --> 00:22:26.870
We've got plenty more firepower.

283
00:22:33.870 --> 00:22:36.380
[GARP]
Still a few buildings left.

284
00:22:37.170 --> 00:22:39.170
I must be losin' my touch.

285
00:22:39.800 --> 00:22:41.170
"Losing your touch"?!

286
00:22:41.170 --> 00:22:43.800
[PIRATE AB]
Quit rubbin' it
in, you old bastard!

287
00:22:44.180 --> 00:22:46.960
[COBY]
– Vice Admiral Garp! – Huh?

288
00:22:47.220 --> 00:22:49.470
Hey! There he is!

289
00:22:50.140 --> 00:22:51.890
You alright, Koby?!

290
00:22:54.140 --> 00:22:56.020
I'm so happy!

291
00:22:56.020 --> 00:22:58.400
I thought my buddy was gonna die!

292
00:22:58.400 --> 00:23:00.030
And once again,

293
00:23:00.030 --> 00:23:01.530
Garp overdid it.

294
00:23:01.530 --> 00:23:04.400
Such a naughty boy, isn't he?

295
00:23:04.400 --> 00:23:08.370
I can't believe he said
Koby is the future of the Navy. As if.

296
00:23:08.370 --> 00:23:10.580
I'll put that kid in his place!

297
00:23:10.580 --> 00:23:16.080
[KUJAKU]
I know you're too spoiled to know better,
but that's not the sort of thing you should say out loud.

298
00:23:16.710 --> 00:23:18.790
Koby!

299
00:23:18.790 --> 00:23:21.090
[MARINE B]
Captain Koby!

300
00:23:21.420 --> 00:23:23.550
[TASHIGI]
Koby!

301
00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:25.260
Tashigi!

302
00:23:25.630 --> 00:23:28.010
Even people who are from SWORD are here!

303
00:23:29.140 --> 00:23:32.100
Hm? What have you got there?
A big ball and chain?

304
00:23:32.100 --> 00:23:33.430
We

305
00:23:33.850 --> 00:23:37.520
had no choice but to take it with us!

306
00:23:37.520 --> 00:23:38.480
Isn't there...

307
00:23:40.860 --> 00:23:42.190
Something

308
00:23:42.780 --> 00:23:44.030
we can...

309
00:23:51.080 --> 00:23:52.080
Hibari!

310
00:23:52.080 --> 00:23:53.290
Hey, buddy!

311
00:23:56.670 --> 00:23:57.960
She's frozen solid?

312
00:24:10.010 --> 00:24:11.260
[GARP]
Kuzan.

313
00:24:11.760 --> 00:24:13.220
Why, Kuzan?

314
00:24:13.560 --> 00:24:14.980
Why are you doing this?

315
00:24:14.980 --> 00:24:17.480
Unfreeze Hibari right now!

316
00:24:17.520 --> 00:24:21.060
[PIRATE AC]
Woohoo! Hell yeah, it's Aokiji!

317
00:24:21.690 --> 00:24:24.190
You guys are dead now!

318
00:24:24.190 --> 00:24:26.030
Go, Kuzan!

319
00:24:27.400 --> 00:24:29.280
[AOKIJI]
Don't get me in trouble, kid.

320
00:24:29.280 --> 00:24:31.200
Can't have you getting away.

321
00:24:31.620 --> 00:24:34.330
How would that look to Teach?

322
00:24:35.040 --> 00:24:40.830
[NARRATOR]
Two years ago, there was a struggle to determine
who would be the next Fleet Admiral at Navy Headquarters.

323
00:24:41.420 --> 00:24:47.510
To that end, Admiral Akainu
and Admiral Aokiji had a duel.

324
00:24:50.940 --> 00:24:56.020
[NARRATOR]
The fight went on for ten days
before a victor was decided.

325
00:24:56.680 --> 00:24:57.730
Akainu stood

326
00:24:59.440 --> 00:25:04.400
Regardless, Aokiji refused
to serve under Akainu as Fleet Admiral,

327
00:25:04.400 --> 00:25:08.110
and so, he resigned.

328
00:25:12.530 --> 00:25:17.500
<b>Some Island, New World</b>

329
00:25:26.300 --> 00:25:28.380
What the hell?

330
00:25:28.720 --> 00:25:30.510
[TOWNSPERSON A]
Blackbeard is here!

331
00:25:30.510 --> 00:25:33.300
[TOWNSPERSON B]
Run!
Get outta town while you can!

332
00:25:33.300 --> 00:25:34.220
Hey!

333
00:25:34.220 --> 00:25:36.430
What is this? What happened here?

334
00:25:36.430 --> 00:25:39.390
Stop! Someone tell me who did this!

335
00:25:43.520 --> 00:25:46.670
[TEACH]
Wait, I know what this is.

336
00:25:47.320 --> 00:25:52.740
I don't even gotta ask. There's only one guy
in the world who could pull this off!

337
00:25:54.700 --> 00:25:56.160
I thought so!

338
00:25:56.160 --> 00:25:58.200
Aokiji!

339
00:26:10.800 --> 00:26:13.430
[TEACH]
What's the big idea, turnin'
my crew into ice cubes?

340
00:26:13.430 --> 00:26:15.850
Fix it!

341
00:26:16.720 --> 00:26:19.310
[AOKIJI]
Why don't you fix your attitude?

342
00:26:20.310 --> 00:26:22.940
[AOKIJI]
Wouldn't do that if I were you.

343
00:26:24.440 --> 00:26:26.730
Your friends'll shatter and die.

344
00:26:28.230 --> 00:26:31.490
C'mon, now. You think I started this fight?

345
00:26:32.740 --> 00:26:35.200
You know what kind of company you keep.

346
00:26:35.950 --> 00:26:38.910
Also, I'm sure you heard the news about me.

347
00:26:39.660 --> 00:26:43.830
I'm in a state of mourning.
You shouldn't test me.

348
00:26:45.880 --> 00:26:48.800
So let's cool it with the demands, shall we?

349
00:27:12.610 --> 00:27:15.070
Who's ready for more?

350
00:27:16.780 --> 00:27:19.870
We can't...

351
00:27:19.870 --> 00:27:22.620
You're not so bad yourself, shitbag!

352
00:27:25.080 --> 00:27:29.070
Okay, before the battle,
what does Akainu say?

353
00:27:31.840 --> 00:27:34.970
"We climbed the ranks together,
now we fight to the death.

354
00:27:34.970 --> 00:27:38.180
I'm starting to feel a hot lump in my throat."

355
00:27:38.890 --> 00:27:41.890
That's what he said.
And you know what I told him?

356
00:27:42.220 --> 00:27:44.930
"No shit, asshole, you're made of magma!"

357
00:27:47.100 --> 00:27:49.310
Look what that bastard did!

358
00:27:52.530 --> 00:27:54.490
Took off my whole damn leg!

359
00:27:55.400 --> 00:27:58.360
So that's what happens when two admirals
decide to throw down, huh?

360
00:27:58.360 --> 00:27:59.910
So'd you pay him back, or what?

361
00:28:00.450 --> 00:28:02.830
Rip off one of his arms, maybe?

362
00:28:03.200 --> 00:28:04.200
[AOKIJI]
Nah.

363
00:28:06.920 --> 00:28:09.540
But he's got some scars to remember me by.

364
00:28:12.130 --> 00:28:16.470
That reminds me, Commodore.
He might know the Man with the Burn Scar.

365
00:28:16.840 --> 00:28:18.970
The what? Who the hell's that?

366
00:28:18.970 --> 00:28:24.770
The deal is, if we wanna make it to Laugh Tale,
We gotta find the four Road Poneglyphs.

367
00:28:26.890 --> 00:28:32.350
Ys know 'em when you see 'em, 'cause they're
bright red. Kaido and Big Mom have one each.

368
00:28:33.190 --> 00:28:37.530
But what about the other two?
They're still a mystery!

369
00:28:37.530 --> 00:28:40.280
We're just hoping fate will guide us to them.

370
00:28:40.280 --> 00:28:41.240
That's right.

371
00:28:41.240 --> 00:28:47.250
Well, we do have one tiny lead. We heard
some man with a burn scar has one of them.

372
00:28:48.960 --> 00:28:50.120
You mean me?

373
00:28:50.120 --> 00:28:52.500
No, not you! You just got that the other day!

374
00:28:57.170 --> 00:28:59.180
Quite the mystery, no?

375
00:29:05.470 --> 00:29:10.310
[LAFITTE]
Rumor has it that the Man
with the Burn Scar sails on a pitch-black ship.

376
00:29:17.280 --> 00:29:24.700
[LAFITTE]
But if anyone approaches it, their ship
will be whisked away, swallowed up by a giant whirlpool.

377
00:29:27.790 --> 00:29:30.500
I'd assume the fellow has a devil fruit power.

378
00:29:31.120 --> 00:29:34.710
[SHIRYU]
Just a hunch,
but I bet the guy is with the Government.

379
00:29:35.210 --> 00:29:38.760
They've got their hands in everything,
and plenty of dark secrets.

380
00:29:38.760 --> 00:29:41.630
They know everyone needs those stones.

381
00:29:41.630 --> 00:29:44.980
If they had one, all they'd have
to do is hold on to it

382
00:29:44.980 --> 00:29:50.840
and we'd be sunk. No pirate could find
their way to Laugh Tale or the One Piece.

383
00:29:51.690 --> 00:29:55.570
The Poneglyphs, huh? Brings back memories.

384
00:29:55.570 --> 00:30:01.240
Hate to break it to ya, but I never saw
a giant red stone in Ohara. I'd remember.

385
00:30:02.860 --> 00:30:04.990
I haven't forgotten a thing about that day.

386
00:30:04.990 --> 00:30:08.240
The day I watched my best friend rebel
against the Government.

387
00:30:08.240 --> 00:30:11.080
And the day that I saw those sad eyes.

388
00:30:11.580 --> 00:30:15.340
When I held that poor, lonely girl's fate in my hands.

389
00:30:17.670 --> 00:30:20.550
Huh? That story sounds boring as all hell!

390
00:30:23.380 --> 00:30:25.600
[LAFITTE]
Commodore, what should we do?

391
00:30:26.600 --> 00:30:30.930
A power like his could be quite useful.
I say we take it while his guard's down.

392
00:30:36.400 --> 00:30:39.360
[AOKIJI]
I heard that, you conniving bastards!

393
00:30:41.570 --> 00:30:45.530
C'mon, then! You wanna know
what it feels like to freeze to death?

394
00:30:49.080 --> 00:30:50.450
Take it easy, buddy!

395
00:30:52.000 --> 00:30:58.470
[AOKIJI]
So the rumors are true. You're hunting people
with strong devil fruit powers, aren't you?

396
00:30:59.210 --> 00:31:02.720
Then try to take mine! I dare you!

397
00:31:06.590 --> 00:31:07.800
Whoa, whoa!

398
00:31:08.680 --> 00:31:09.930
Listen to me!

399
00:31:09.930 --> 00:31:12.680
My crew members were getting
carried away, that's all!

400
00:31:13.310 --> 00:31:15.850
Let me apologize on their behalf.

401
00:31:15.850 --> 00:31:17.980
I don't wanna steal your power.

402
00:31:17.980 --> 00:31:20.440
I want you to join my crew!

403
00:31:21.400 --> 00:31:24.650
Are you nuts? An ex-Marine?

404
00:31:24.650 --> 00:31:27.620
Why not? You're out of a job now, right?

405
00:31:27.620 --> 00:31:29.620
You got any place to go?

406
00:31:29.620 --> 00:31:31.620
Anything you're planning to do?

407
00:31:31.620 --> 00:31:34.040
Not gonna be defending justice anymore.

408
00:31:35.080 --> 00:31:37.210
Ha! Guess I've sunk pretty low, huh?

409
00:31:37.210 --> 00:31:41.090
A good-for-nothing pirate's worried
about the state of my employment.

410
00:31:41.090 --> 00:31:44.300
[TEACH]
Men like us will find
trouble anywhere we go.

411
00:31:44.920 --> 00:31:48.050
Can't run, so you might
as well face it head-on.

412
00:31:48.050 --> 00:31:53.220
What flag will you fly? When you put your life on the line,
what will you be fighting for?

413
00:31:53.220 --> 00:31:54.640
Tell me!

414
00:31:56.020 --> 00:31:59.020
I've got my own brand
of justice, my own code!

415
00:31:59.020 --> 00:32:01.860
This won't be nothing
like the Navy, I promise you!

416
00:32:01.860 --> 00:32:03.190
Yeah, I'm sure!

417
00:32:03.190 --> 00:32:08.200
But I'll still get stabbed straight in the back!
You think sharin' a couple of drinks means I can trust you?

418
00:32:08.200 --> 00:32:09.570
Of course not!

419
00:32:09.570 --> 00:32:12.450
I don't think you understand
how pirates work!

420
00:32:12.450 --> 00:32:16.460
We're not here to make friends!
We're a crew, but we're not buddy-buddy!

421
00:32:21.630 --> 00:32:23.840
We all have a common goal!

422
00:32:26.510 --> 00:32:30.680
All pirates need is an alignment of interests!

423
00:32:33.560 --> 00:32:36.680
You're free now, Kuzan. Your choice.

424
00:32:38.190 --> 00:32:40.100
What do you really want?

425
00:32:54.660 --> 00:32:56.290
Stop this, Kuzan!

426
00:32:56.750 --> 00:32:58.580
Thaw Hibari out right now!

427
00:32:59.120 --> 00:33:00.920
Let Koby escape from here!

428
00:33:00.920 --> 00:33:03.630
Come back to the Navy!

429
00:33:06.380 --> 00:33:11.510
Y'never change, huh? Can't stop to think.
You just run your mouth.

430
00:33:15.220 --> 00:33:19.310
But I'm afraid I can't help you today, Garp!

431
00:33:20.230 --> 00:33:22.020
[AOKIJI]
You've always been straightforward.

432
00:33:22.900 --> 00:33:24.730
I admire that.

433
00:33:25.360 --> 00:33:29.650
You inspired me. So I'm livin'
the way I want to now!

434
00:33:26.650 --> 00:33:29.650
<b>Kuzan
Captain of the Tenth Ship
Blackbeard Pirates</b>

435
00:33:34.870 --> 00:33:36.240
You damn fool.

436
00:33:52.970 --> 00:33:54.600
Ice Ball!

437
00:34:01.770 --> 00:34:03.730
[COBY]
Vice Admiral Garp!

438
00:34:05.900 --> 00:34:07.730
Vice Admiral!

439
00:34:11.200 --> 00:34:13.820
[AOKIJI]
Your old student
and your new student...

440
00:34:14.410 --> 00:34:18.910
Would you do anything
to save Koby, even if it kills me?

441
00:34:20.620 --> 00:34:23.610
Heh. What are you doing,
bringing up the past?

442
00:34:24.460 --> 00:34:27.710
I taught you to live in the moment, didn't I?

443
00:34:32.000 --> 00:34:34.180
How the hell did he break free?!

444
00:34:54.410 --> 00:34:56.160
Here's another lesson!

445
00:35:19.350 --> 00:35:21.560
Men who waver...

446
00:35:23.310 --> 00:35:25.040
...are weak!

447
00:35:26.480 --> 00:35:29.900
Come on! Blue Hole!

448
00:35:58.890 --> 00:36:04.060
<b>Winner Island
New World</b>

449
00:35:58.890 --> 00:36:02.600
[NARRATOR]
On the coast of Winter Island...

450
00:36:39.390 --> 00:36:44.270
Now that your ship is out of the picture,
you haven't just lost your right to call yourself a pirate,

451
00:36:44.770 --> 00:36:47.480
you've lost your only escape.

452
00:36:48.100 --> 00:36:54.360
You stole 100 hearts that day at Rocky Port.
You had to expect some kinda payback from me!

453
00:36:54.360 --> 00:36:58.950
Those poor pirates back at my base, living
every damn day in fear!

454
00:36:59.320 --> 00:37:05.540
So I think I'll bring them back your heart as a gift!
Bet that'll have the sad bastards jumpin' for joy!

455
00:37:12.420 --> 00:37:14.670
Oh, wow, you made this for me?

456
00:37:14.670 --> 00:37:18.630
But I haven't been able to test it,
so I can't guarantee it'll work.

457
00:37:24.390 --> 00:37:26.020
Let me think.

458
00:37:26.020 --> 00:37:30.390
We could sell your Fruit,
but I think I could put it to better use.

459
00:37:30.390 --> 00:37:33.610
They say it can grant
someone eternal life, right?

460
00:37:46.240 --> 00:37:48.680
[BEPO]
That's my captain!

461
00:38:04.720 --> 00:38:06.850
It can't be!

462
00:38:06.850 --> 00:38:09.310
Sulong? But how? The moon isn't even out!

463
00:39:00.030 --> 00:39:02.320
Damn it! They're headed to the sea!

464
00:39:02.320 --> 00:39:04.530
Get them, now!

465
00:39:11.500 --> 00:39:14.080
[LAW]
Take me back, Bepo.

466
00:39:18.540 --> 00:39:22.840
They're my friends. I can't leave them.

467
00:39:22.840 --> 00:39:24.590
I'm sorry, Captain!

468
00:39:24.780 --> 00:39:27.720
We can't risk it! But your crew was

469
00:39:27.720 --> 00:39:30.510
forged in the cold waters of the north!

470
00:39:32.520 --> 00:39:35.900
Have faith in them! Through every fight,

471
00:39:35.900 --> 00:39:37.190
they've held strong!

472
00:39:38.480 --> 00:39:40.980
They won't die here!

473
00:39:46.740 --> 00:39:49.490
[BEPO]
We've overcome so much together!

474
00:39:51.580 --> 00:39:53.450
[BEPO]
We have to survive!

475
00:39:54.540 --> 00:39:57.120
all of us.

476
00:40:05.880 --> 00:40:07.470
[BEPO]
Don't die, Captain!

477
00:40:08.840 --> 00:40:10.850
We need you!

478
00:40:14.930 --> 00:40:20.830
[NARRATOR]
The battle at Winner Island,
in the New World, came to an end.

479
00:40:28.320 --> 00:40:33.410
[NARRATOR]
Blackbeard destroyed the Polar Tang,
the submarine of the Heart Pirates,

480
00:40:33.410 --> 00:40:36.480
and it sank into the sea.

481
00:40:38.370 --> 00:40:43.260
The Heart Pirates, led by Trafalgar Law,

482
00:40:43.750 --> 00:40:45.260
were defeated.

483
00:40:54.210 --> 00:40:59.300
Running so long lost track of just how long its been

484
00:41:00.150 --> 00:41:06.660
Collected scars while striving not even trying beneath my skin

485
00:41:07.160 --> 00:41:14.080
But in the back of my head the dream is not dead I remember a map

486
00:41:14.160 --> 00:41:20.370
to a treasure still gleaming its within our grasp

487
00:41:20.510 --> 00:41:27.280
Can you feel my heart Feelings I impart

488
00:41:27.240 --> 00:41:34.390
The promises are there theyre deep down but still primed to share

489
00:41:34.520 --> 00:41:43.500
Peerless dreams kept close the dreams that always matter most

490
00:41:43.680 --> 00:41:49.250
Before we set sail why not raise a toast

491
00:41:49.370 --> 00:41:56.280
So I pen this note to you Dear sunrise Ill see you soon

492
00:41:56.440 --> 00:42:03.470
See the smile I saw the day that I sang this song to you

493
00:42:03.450 --> 00:42:10.520
And regardless of our age these memries will still remain

494
00:42:10.420 --> 00:42:17.630
Wont forget until this wish makes it to you
